{
  "description": "Which composites a consumer forms from a descriptor (il.md section 10, K-1..K-4, G-1..G-5, O-5, X-1). For each case: `composites` lists the composites that MUST form, in any order, as {kind, group (null for the device's own), roles: the required roles with the property carrying each, optional: roles the consumer MAY also use}. A consumer's composite for that kind and group MUST contain every entry of `roles` and MAY add only entries of `optional`. `no_composite` lists kinds (of the device or of a group) that MUST NOT form one. What entity a consumer builds from a composite is its own business. A descriptor is valid against the schema unless its case says `schema_valid: false` (it is there to test a consumer's tolerance).",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a light is on plus whichever level roles it has (K-1)",
      "descriptor": {
        "il": 0,
        "id": "dev1",
        "kind": "light",
        "props": {
          "pw": {
            "type": "binary",
            "rw": true,
            "role": "on"
          },
          "br": {
            "type": "number",
            "rw": true,
            "role": "brightness",
            "unit": "%",
            "min": 1,
            "max": 100
          },
          "ct": {
            "type": "number",
            "rw": true,
            "role": "color_temperature",
            "unit": "K",
            "min": 2700,
            "max": 6500
          },
          "fx": {
            "type": "select",
            "rw": true,
            "options": [
              "a",
              "b"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "composites": [
        {
          "kind": "light",
          "group": null,
          "roles": {
            "on": "pw"
          },
          "optional": {
            "brightness": "br",
            "color_temperature": "ct"
          }
        }
      ],
      "no_composite": []
    },
